# Inside a barn (barn.c). Six stalls along the back: the manger behind each stall (row 2) fills with hay
# once that animal is fed; cows and sheep stand in their stall (row 3). The hay stack fills the mangers.
# Walls and floor are drawn in the farm's building style (barn.c swaps the CLASSIC tiles).
# The doorway leads back out to the barn door, wherever that barn stands. (File name sorts after town.)
map BARN set=INTERIOR w=12 h=9 music=NONE
key L WALL_SIDE_L block
key R WALL_SIDE_R block
key T BARN_BEAM block
key l BARN_BEAM_LAMP block
key W BARN_WALL_CLASSIC block
key . BARN_FLOOR_CLASSIC walk
key M MANGER_EMPTY block
key S STALL block
key X WALL_FRONT block
key C WALL_CORNER_L block
key D WALL_CORNER_R block
key [ BARN_DOOR_L walk
key ] BARN_DOOR_R walk
grid
LTTlTTTTlTTR
LWWWWWWWWWWR
LMMMMMM....R
LSSSSSS....R
L..........R
L..........R
L..........R
L..........R
CXXXX[]XXXXD
place BARN_TOOLS 7 2
place HAY_STACK 8 2
place MILK_CANS 10 2
warp 5 8 FARM 0 0 down
warp 6 8 FARM 0 0 down
